  "result": "Subcommands now pick up their `default_map` defaults. The fix is in the `Context` constructor in `src/click/core.py`, and the full test suite passes.\n\nA subcommand's context was inheriting the parent's whole `default_map` instead of the entry for its own name. A map like `{\"sub\": {\"n\": 5}}` was therefore looked up with `n` at the top level and never matched. It now takes `parent.default_map.get(info_name)`.\n\nI checked it with a group and a `sub` command with `--n` defaulting to 1. Invoking `sub` with `default_map={\"sub\": {\"n\": 5}}` now prints 5. I didn't add a regression test for it.",
